# Regression: full baremetal triples whose arch field carries an ISA profile
# (armv7a/armv7r/armv8r/armv5te/thumbv7a ...) reached backend admission
# verbatim and failed with BACKEND_PLUGIN_TARGET; only short names worked.
use std.spec
use std.spec.step
use compiler.driver.driver_backend_plugin_selection.{driver_backend_plugin_target}

describe "baremetal target triple normalization":
    it "maps ISA-profile ARM arch fields to arm":
        step("arm/thumb profiles are one builtin target")
        expect(driver_backend_plugin_target("armv7a-none-eabi")).to_equal("arm")
        expect(driver_backend_plugin_target("armv7r-none-eabihf")).to_equal("arm")
        expect(driver_backend_plugin_target("armv8r-none-eabihf")).to_equal("arm")
        expect(driver_backend_plugin_target("armv5te-none-eabi")).to_equal("arm")
        expect(driver_backend_plugin_target("thumbv7a-none-eabi")).to_equal("arm")
        expect(driver_backend_plugin_target("thumbv8m.main-none-eabihf")).to_equal("arm")

    it "keeps the other common baremetal triples":
        expect(driver_backend_plugin_target("riscv64gc-unknown-none-elf")).to_equal("riscv64")
        expect(driver_backend_plugin_target("riscv32imac-unknown-none-elf")).to_equal("riscv32")
        expect(driver_backend_plugin_target("aarch64-unknown-none-softfloat")).to_equal("aarch64")
        expect(driver_backend_plugin_target("x86_64-unknown-none")).to_equal("x86_64")
        expect(driver_backend_plugin_target("i686-unknown-none")).to_equal("x86")
